# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces the revised MD17 data set (100,000 structures per molecule recomputed at PBE/def2-SVP); the level of theory is entered in the data-set registry from this paper. The origin-paper stub of this paper is removed from origin-papers.csv now that it is encoded.
# - The models are kernel ridge regression with the FCHL19 representation, recorded as a new registry method FCHL19 (introduced elsewhere; not in the corpus).
# - Only N = 1,000 of the eight training-set sizes of Table S1 is encoded; the other sizes and the small-organic-molecule models are learning curves.
# - Errors are averages over the outer 5-fold cross-validation (Sec. 4.1).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/christensen2020.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

